  "question": {
    "text": "When a spring is stretched by $10 \\mathrm{cm}$, the potential energy stored is $E$. When the spring is stretched by $10 \\mathrm{cm}$ more, the potential energy stored in the spring becomes",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AVQcu",
      "text": "$2 E$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TygiJ",
      "text": "$4 E$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ybd3u",
      "text": "$6 E$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "HW5qD",
      "text": "$10 E$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For 1st situation,\r\n$$\r\nE=\\frac{1}{2} k\\left(10 \\times 10^{-2}\\right)^{2}\r\n$$\r\nFor 2nd situation,\r\n$$\r\nE^{\\prime}=\\frac{1}{2} k\\left(20 \\times 10^{-2}\\right)^{2}\r\n$$\r\nOn comparing Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get\r\n$$\r\nE^{\\prime}=4 E\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
